export const LIVE_BASKET_TEXTS = {"PA-BAA-2026-11":{"title":"PlotArt Artist Basket Addendum","kind":"artist_basket_addendum","html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en-IE\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>PlotArt Artist Basket Addendum · PA-BAA-2026-11</title><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\">\n<style>\n:root{color-scheme:light}body{margin:0;background:#F4F1EC;color:#1B1C1E;font:16px/1.6 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1rem 4rem}.eyebrow{margin:0;color:#AE6245;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.8rem}\nh1{font:400 2.1rem/1.15 Georgia,serif;margin:.3rem 0 .4rem}.sub{margin:0 0 2rem;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.95rem}\nh2{font:400 1.3rem/1.3 Georgia,serif;margin:2.2rem 0 .7rem}p{margin:0 0 .8rem}.cl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem minmax(0,1fr)}\n.cl .n{font-weight:700}ul{margin:0 0 .9rem 3rem;padding-left:0;list-style:none}li{margin:0 0 .35rem}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:.6rem 0 1.4rem;font-size:.92rem}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #D8D1C7;padding:.55rem .65rem}\nthead th{background:#EFEBE5}tbody th{font-weight:400;width:60%}footer{margin-top:3rem;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid #C9C2B8;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.85rem}\n@media (max-width:30rem){.cl{grid-template-columns:2.6rem minmax(0,1fr)}ul{margin-left:2.6rem}h1{font-size:1.75rem}}\n@media print{body{background:#fff}main{padding:0}}\n</style></head>\n<body><main><article data-doc=\"PA-BAA-2026-11\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">PLOTART</p>\n<h1>Artist Basket Addendum</h1>\n<p class=\"sub\">Identifier PA-BAA-2026-11 · Text of 21 November 2026</p>\n<h2 id=\"0-how-this-addendum-relates-to-the-artist-s-agreement\">0. How this addendum relates to the artist's agreement</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c0.1\"><span class=\"n\">0.1</span><span><strong>This addendum is optional.</strong> It applies only to basket orders: purchases of the artist's artworks made by a buyer through the PlotArt basket, alone or together with other artists' works. It sits beside the artist's PlotArt agreement (PA-FAA-2026-11 Founding Artist Agreement or PA-GAA-2026-11 Gallery Artist Agreement), the Gallery Publication and Image Licence PA-GPIL-2026-11 and the Payment Pilot Addendum PA-PAY-2026-11. An artist who does not accept it loses nothing: their gallery listing, enquiries, direct sales and any quote under PA-PAY continue exactly as before.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c0.2\"><span class=\"n\">0.2</span><span><strong>Nothing in this addendum reduces any right the artist has under their agreement.</strong> In particular:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) <strong>Founding Artists.</strong> Every Founding Enquiry stays commission-free permanently, and commission can arise only under separate commission terms that the artist has expressly accepted (PA-FAA cl. 3, 5 and 6). This addendum is not such terms. <strong>PlotArt charges no commission and no fee of any kind on a basket order that carries no commission under the artist's agreement.</strong> The only cost on such an order is Stripe's own processing fee, which applies only if the artist gives the separate processing consent in clause 4 and which the artist can avoid at any time by withdrawing it;</li><li>(b) <strong>Gallery Artists.</strong> The commission rate, Commission Base and refund rules remain those of PA-GAA cl. 5 and 9, including that the artist keeps at least 85% of the Commission Base. On a basket order, as on a pilot order, the artist's combined deduction for PlotArt commission and Stripe's payment processing is never more than that commission (clause 3.3);</li><li>(c) commission is never charged on delivery, packing, transport, insurance, installation or import costs;</li><li>(d) if any part of this addendum could be read as reducing such a right, the artist's agreement prevails on that point.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c0.3\"><span class=\"n\">0.3</span><span><strong>How this addendum fits the artist's agreement.</strong></span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) For a Gallery Artist, this addendum is a written variation under PA-GAA clause 13, applying only to basket orders. For those orders only: PA-GAA clause 4.2 applies as modified by clauses 2, 5 and 6 of this addendum; PlotArt's commission is collected under clause 3.2 instead of being reported and invoiced under PA-GAA clauses 8.1 to 8.4; and commission is returned under clause 7, within the period in PA-GAA clause 9. PA-GAA continues to apply in full to every other sale, and to basket orders in every respect not changed here.</li><li>(b) For a Founding Artist, this addendum changes nothing in PA-FAA. It introduces no commission and no compulsory fee (PA-FAA cl. 3 and 13.2). Taking part, and giving the processing consent, are the artist's free choice and can be withdrawn at any time.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c0.4\"><span class=\"n\">0.4</span><span><strong>PA-PAY clauses that apply to basket orders.</strong> To take part in the basket, the artist must also have joined the payment pilot under PA-PAY-2026-11, which provides the artist's Stripe account, seller information and records. The following clauses of PA-PAY apply to every basket order as if it were a pilot order, with the changes made in this addendum:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) clause 2 (the artist is the seller; seller information; trader declaration; the artist's Stripe account; receiving notices);</li><li>(b) clauses 3.2 to 3.9 (collection of commission, Stripe processing fees and their reimbursement on commission orders, VAT, the artist's statement, tax);</li><li>(c) clause 5.2 (payouts);</li><li>(d) clause 6.3 and 6.4 (dispatch evidence; buyer's rights not depending on claims);</li><li>(e) clauses 7.1 to 7.9 (cancellations, returns, refunds, disputes and negative balances), reading &quot;Buyer Purchase Terms PA-BPT-2026-11&quot; as &quot;Basket Purchase Terms PA-BBT-2026-11&quot; and &quot;quote&quot; as &quot;basket page and purchase confirmation&quot;;</li><li>(f) clause 8 (records) and clause 9 (information shared), with the additions in clause 9 of this addendum;</li><li>(g) clause 10 (test mode and live payments).</li></ul>\n<p>PA-PAY clause 1.3, which excludes multi-artwork orders and sales that carry no commission from the pilot, does not apply to basket orders. It continues to apply to quotes under PA-PAY.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-what-the-basket-is\">1. What the basket is</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.1\"><span class=\"n\">1.1</span><span>The basket lets a buyer buy, online and without a quote, one or more of the artist's available artworks for which the artist has a current delivery offer (clause 5), alone or together with other artists' works.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.2\"><span class=\"n\">1.2</span><span>The buyer enters their card once. PlotArt then makes a separate card payment for each artwork, directly to its artist's own Stripe account (clause 6). Two artworks by the same artist are two separate payments and two separate orders.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.3\"><span class=\"n\">1.3</span><span><strong>Scope.</strong> The basket covers existing original artworks priced from EUR 1.00 to EUR 9,999.99, sold in euro, for delivery in the Republic of Ireland. It does not cover prints, commissions of new work, hire, discounts, gift cards or instalments. PlotArt will not accept a basket that would bring a buyer's apparently linked purchases through PlotArt to EUR 10,000 or more in twelve months (PA-PAY 1.4 applies). These are limits on the scope of the basket, not a statement about anyone's legal obligations.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.4\"><span class=\"n\">1.4</span><span><strong>Taking part is optional.</strong> An artist who has joined the payment pilot (clause 0.4) joins the basket by accepting this addendum in PlotArt Studio, and can leave at any time there (clause 10). For a Founding Artist, joining the payment pilot changes nothing in PA-FAA (PA-PAY 0.4(b)).</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-the-artist-is-the-seller\">2. The artist is the seller</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.1\"><span class=\"n\">2.1</span><span>The artist is the seller of each of their artworks bought through the basket and contracts directly with the buyer. PlotArt introduces the buyer, provides the basket and checkout and coordinates the payments. It is not the seller, and does not take ownership or possession of any artwork.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.2\"><span class=\"n\">2.2</span><span><strong>Seller information and trader declaration.</strong> PA-PAY clauses 2.2 and 2.3 apply. The law requires a buyer to be given the seller's identity, the geographical address at which the seller is established, and contact details before paying. Because the basket page can be opened by anyone, PlotArt shows the artist's seller information there only after the artist has separately confirmed, in PlotArt Studio, that it may be shown before payment. The confirmation is recorded with the exact information it covers; if the artist changes that information, their artworks are withdrawn from the basket until the artist confirms again. The VAT number is shown only if the artist is registered. An artwork cannot be offered in the basket while the artist's seller information, trader declaration or this confirmation is missing. The confirmation statement is:</span></p>\n<p>I confirm that my seller information — legal name and any trading name, the geographical address at which I am established (and any separate returns address), my email and telephone for buyers, and my VAT number if I am registered — may be shown to anyone viewing the PlotArt basket before they buy one of my artworks, and in each purchase confirmation. I understand that the law requires buyers to be given the address at which I am established before they pay. If I do not want that address shown in this way, I will not confirm, and my artworks will not be offered in the basket; my gallery listing, enquiries and direct sales are unaffected.</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.3\"><span class=\"n\">2.3</span><span><strong>Buyer terms.</strong> The buyer's rights are set out in the Basket Purchase Terms PA-BBT-2026-11. The artist will honour them for each of their artworks, including:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) the buyer may cancel one artwork and keep others (PA-BBT 7.1);</li><li>(b) where the buyer bought two or more of the artist's artworks in one basket and they arrive separately, the cancellation period for each runs from receipt of the last of them (PA-BBT 7.2). Artworks by other artists in the same basket do not affect the artist's cancellation period;</li><li>(c) if the artist cannot deliver within the stated window, the buyer may end the contract for that artwork and be refunded in full (PA-BBT 6.2).</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"3-commission-processing-fees-and-tax\">3. Commission, processing fees and tax</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.1\"><span class=\"n\">3.1</span><span><strong>PlotArt commission on a basket order is exactly what the artist's agreement provides:</strong></span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) none on a sale arising from a Founding Enquiry (PA-FAA cl. 5);</li><li>(b) for a Founding Artist, none unless separate commission terms that the artist has expressly accepted were in effect when the buyer was introduced (PA-FAA cl. 6);</li><li>(c) for a Gallery Artist, the rate and Commission Base in PA-GAA cl. 5 (currently 15% of the artwork price).</li></ul>\n<p>Commission is never charged on delivery, packing, transport, insurance, installation or import costs. PlotArt charges the buyer no fee.</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.2\"><span class=\"n\">3.2</span><span><strong>Which rate applies.</strong> PlotArt records, for each basket order, whether it carries commission and on what basis, and shows it in the artist's statement. Where PlotArt cannot show that a sale by a Founding Artist carries commission under terms the artist expressly accepted, it carries none (PA-FAA cl. 5.6).</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.3\"><span class=\"n\">3.3</span><span><strong>Orders that carry commission.</strong> PA-PAY clauses 3.2 to 3.8 apply in full. PlotArt receives its commission as a Stripe application fee on that artwork's payment, reimburses the artist Stripe's actual processing fee on that payment and the VAT Stripe charges on it, within the time limits in PA-PAY 3.3, and pays any shortfall directly under PA-PAY 3.5. The artist's combined deduction for commission and Stripe's processing is never more than the commission.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.4\"><span class=\"n\">3.4</span><span><strong>Orders that carry no commission.</strong> On a basket order that carries no PlotArt commission:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) PlotArt receives nothing: no commission, no application fee and no other fee;</li><li>(b) Stripe charges its processing fee on the whole amount the buyer pays for that artwork, including delivery, and deducts it, and any VAT Stripe charges on it, from the artist's Stripe balance. PlotArt does not reimburse it, because there is no application fee from which to do so;</li><li>(c) such an order can be made only if the artist has given the processing consent in clause 4, and it remains in effect when the buyer checks out.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.5\"><span class=\"n\">3.5</span><span><strong>Fees on payments that are not taken.</strong> If a basket is cancelled after an artwork's payment has been authorised but before it is taken (clause 6.4), no payment is made to the artist and no commission is due. If Stripe charges the artist any fee for that authorisation, PlotArt reimburses it under PA-PAY 3.5.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.6\"><span class=\"n\">3.6</span><span><strong>VAT and tax.</strong> PA-PAY clauses 3.6 and 3.9 apply. The artist remains responsible for any VAT or other tax on the sale of each artwork, and for any invoice or receipt the law requires the artist to give the buyer.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.7\"><span class=\"n\">3.7</span><span><strong>Examples (illustration only).</strong> Stripe's published standard pricing for EEA businesses on 20 November 2026 is used (standard EEA cards 1.5% + €0.25), with VAT on Stripe's fee shown for a Stripe account based in Ireland (PA-PAY 3.6). PlotArt and the artist use the amounts Stripe actually charges.</span></p>\n<p>Example 1: a Gallery Artist on 15% commission; a EUR 1,000 artwork with EUR 75 delivery in a basket; standard EEA card.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Buyer pays for this artwork</th><th scope=\"col\">€1,075.00</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">PlotArt commission (15% of the artwork only)</th><td>− €150.00</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Stripe processing fee on €1,075, and VAT on it</th><td>− €20.15</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Reimbursed by PlotArt (fee and VAT)</th><td>+ €20.15</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Artist's net proceeds</th><td>€925.00</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Example 2: a Founding Artist; a sale that carries no commission; the same artwork, delivery and card; processing consent given.</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Buyer pays for this artwork</th><th scope=\"col\">€1,075.00</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">PlotArt commission</th><td>€0.00</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Stripe processing fee on €1,075</th><td>− €16.38</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">VAT charged by Stripe on that fee</th><td>− €3.77</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Artist's net proceeds</th><td>€1,054.85</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>With other cards the processing fee is higher (PA-PAY 3.7). A direct sale arranged by the artist outside PlotArt carries no PlotArt charge of any kind.</p>\n<h2 id=\"4-processing-consent-for-orders-that-carry-no-commission\">4. Processing consent for orders that carry no commission</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.1\"><span class=\"n\">4.1</span><span><strong>What the consent is.</strong> A Founding Artist, or any artist whose sale would carry no commission, may agree that their commission-free artworks can be bought through the basket on the basis that the artist bears Stripe's actual processing fee on those payments (clause 3.4). PlotArt asks for this consent separately from acceptance of this addendum, with its own statement and tick box, and records the artist, the account that gave it, the version and fingerprint of this addendum, the statement shown, the time and whether it is given or withdrawn. A consent counts only for the version of this addendum it names, and only in live mode if given in live mode.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.2\"><span class=\"n\">4.2</span><span><strong>Without the consent,</strong> the artist's commission-free artworks are not offered in the basket. Buyers can still enquire about them, and the artist sells them directly, commission-free and with no PlotArt charge, as before. The artist's commission-bearing artworks, if any, can still be offered in the basket.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.3\"><span class=\"n\">4.3</span><span><strong>Withdrawing the consent.</strong> The artist can withdraw the consent at any time in PlotArt Studio. From then, their commission-free artworks are no longer offered in the basket. A basket already being paid when the consent is withdrawn is completed on the basis that applied when the buyer checked out.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.4\"><span class=\"n\">4.4</span><span><strong>The consent does not change commission.</strong> It is not commission terms under PA-FAA cl. 6, and it cannot make any sale, including any sale arising from a Founding Enquiry, carry PlotArt commission.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.5\"><span class=\"n\">4.5</span><span><strong>The consent statement.</strong> The statement shown to the artist, with an unticked box, is:</span></p>\n<p>I agree that buyers may buy my artworks that carry no PlotArt commission through the PlotArt basket, under the Artist Basket Addendum PA-BAA-2026-11. I understand that:</p>\n<p>• PlotArt charges 0% commission on these sales during my agreed commission-free period, and takes no fee of any kind from them;</p>\n<p>• each payment goes to my own Stripe account, and Stripe deducts its actual card processing fee, and any VAT it charges on that fee, from my Stripe balance (for example about 1.5% + €0.25 for a standard EEA card; more for premium, UK and international cards). PlotArt does not reimburse it;</p>\n<p>• if I refund a buyer, Stripe does not return its processing fee; if a buyer disputes a payment, Stripe may also charge me its dispute fees;</p>\n<p>• I can withdraw this consent at any time in PlotArt Studio. My commission-free artworks are then no longer offered in the basket; baskets already being paid are completed;</p>\n<p>• declining or withdrawing this consent does not affect my gallery listing, enquiries, direct sales or my Founding Artist Agreement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"5-delivery-offers-and-availability\">5. Delivery offers and availability</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.1\"><span class=\"n\">5.1</span><span><strong>The delivery offer.</strong> An artwork is offered in the basket only while the artist has a current delivery offer for it, approved by the artist in PlotArt Studio. The delivery offer states, for delivery anywhere in the Republic of Ireland:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) the delivery charge, which the buyer pays in full to the artist;</li><li>(b) who packs, who books and contracts with the transporter, who pays for transport, and any installation;</li><li>(c) the delivery window, tracking, and whether a signed receipt and condition photographs are provided;</li><li>(d) the transit insurance: the insurer and who holds the cover, the covered value (at least the artwork price) and valuation basis, any excess and the main exclusions, the period of cover (from collection to signed delivery) and the claims contact;</li><li>(e) the return arrangements in PA-PAY 7.2: how the artwork would be returned, the returns address, the cost of return or a reasonable estimate of the maximum, and who arranges it.</li></ul>\n<p>The carrier's limited liability alone is not accepted as transit insurance.</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.2\"><span class=\"n\">5.2</span><span><strong>The delivery offer is the artist's approval.</strong> By approving a delivery offer, the artist confirms that the artwork is available and not promised elsewhere, that its description (location, condition, framing and glazing, dimensions and weight) is accurate, and that they will sell and deliver it as offered, at the gallery price, to any buyer who completes a basket. This takes the place, for basket orders, of approving each quote under PA-PAY 4.2. Any change to the offer creates a new version, which the artist approves again; a basket already being paid uses the version shown to the buyer.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.3\"><span class=\"n\">5.3</span><span><strong>Keeping it current.</strong> The artist keeps the availability, price and description of each offered artwork, and its delivery offer, accurate and up to date. The artist can withdraw a delivery offer at any time; the artwork is then no longer offered in the basket, except to a buyer whose basket is already being paid.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.4\"><span class=\"n\">5.4</span><span><strong>One original.</strong> While an artwork is offered in the basket, the artist will not sell or promise it elsewhere without first withdrawing its delivery offer or recording the sale in PlotArt Studio straight away. Once a buyer selects &quot;Checkout&quot;, PlotArt's systems hold the artwork for that buyer for the checkout period, currently 31 minutes, plus 15 minutes for Stripe's confirmation, and for up to 30 minutes more while the buyer's bank asks them to confirm a payment. If, exceptionally, a payment is taken for an artwork the artist had already sold another way, the artist refunds that buyer in full (PA-BBT 5.3).</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"6-how-payment-is-taken\">6. How payment is taken</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.1\"><span class=\"n\">6.1</span><span><strong>Authority.</strong> The artist authorises PlotArt, for each basket order for one of the artist's artworks:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) to have Stripe make a copy, on the artist's Stripe account, of the card the buyer entered once on Stripe's page, for use only for that buyer's payments to the artist in that basket;</li><li>(b) to create, on the artist's Stripe account, a card payment for exactly the artwork price and delivery charge shown to the buyer;</li><li>(c) to have the payment authorised first, and to take it only once every payment in the basket has been authorised;</li><li>(d) to cancel the authorisation if any payment in the basket cannot be authorised, if the buyer does not confirm a payment their bank asks them to confirm within 30 minutes, or if the basket is cancelled before payment is taken;</li><li>(e) to receive PlotArt's commission, if any, from that payment as a Stripe application fee;</li><li>(f) to issue refunds from that payment on the artist's instruction or with the artist's agreement (PA-PAY 7.4).</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.2\"><span class=\"n\">6.2</span><span><strong>All or nothing.</strong> No payment in a basket is taken until every payment in it has been authorised. If any cannot be, none is taken and every authorisation is cancelled. An artist is not paid, and owes nothing, for a basket that was not completed.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.3\"><span class=\"n\">6.3</span><span><strong>An order is complete</strong> only when Stripe confirms to PlotArt that the payment for that artwork has been taken. PlotArt then marks the artwork sold in PlotArt Studio, where the artist sees the order, the buyer's name and delivery address, and the delivery offer version that applies.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.4\"><span class=\"n\">6.4</span><span><strong>If a payment is taken but the basket cannot be completed.</strong> If, exceptionally, one or more payments in a basket have been taken but another cannot be, PlotArt tells the affected artists and the buyer straight away. Each order whose payment was taken stands as a completed sale of that artwork, and the buyer may cancel it under PA-BBT section 7 at no return cost if the artwork has not been dispatched; the artist then refunds the buyer in full. Commission on such a refund is returned in full under clause 7.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.5\"><span class=\"n\">6.5</span><span><strong>Payouts</strong> from the artist's Stripe balance follow the artist's Stripe payout schedule. PlotArt does not hold the money, does not delay payouts until delivery and does not offer escrow.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"7-cancellations-returns-refunds-and-disputes\">7. Cancellations, returns, refunds and disputes</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.1\"><span class=\"n\">7.1</span><span>PA-PAY clauses 7.1 to 7.9 apply to each basket order separately. A buyer's cancellation, return, refund or dispute for one artwork does not affect any other order in the basket.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.2\"><span class=\"n\">7.2</span><span><strong>Commission when a buyer is refunded.</strong> On an order that carries commission, PlotArt returns commission as PA-GAA cl. 9 and PA-PAY 7.7 require. On an order that carries no commission there is no commission to return, and Stripe does not return its processing fee on a refunded payment.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.3\"><span class=\"n\">7.3</span><span><strong>Disputes.</strong> PA-PAY 7.8 applies. Stripe's dispute fees are not reimbursed by PlotArt, on any order. PlotArt provides the order record, the basket page details shown to the buyer, the buyer's acceptance of PA-BBT and the delivery evidence it holds.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"8-dispatch-and-delivery\">8. Dispatch and delivery</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.1\"><span class=\"n\">8.1</span><span>The artist dispatches each artwork as stated in its delivery offer, within its delivery window, and records the dispatch and delivery evidence in PlotArt Studio: tracking, a signed receipt and condition photographs, where the offer provides for them.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.2\"><span class=\"n\">8.2</span><span>The transit insurance stated in the delivery offer must be in place for each shipment, and its confirmation reference is recorded in PlotArt Studio before dispatch.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.3\"><span class=\"n\">8.3</span><span>If the artist cannot dispatch within the delivery window, the artist tells the buyer and PlotArt straight away (PA-BBT 6.2).</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"9-records-and-information\">9. Records and information</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.1\"><span class=\"n\">9.1</span><span>PA-PAY clauses 8 and 9 apply to each basket order, with these additions:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) PlotArt keeps the basket record: the artworks, the amounts and basket page details shown to the buyer, the buyer's acceptance of PA-BBT, each authorisation, payment and cancellation, and the delivery offer version used;</li><li>(b) PlotArt shares with the artist the buyer's name and delivery address, and the buyer's email address where needed for delivery or a return. It does not tell the artist what the buyer bought from other artists;</li><li>(c) Stripe saves the buyer's card on PlotArt's Stripe account for the basket and copies it to the artist's Stripe account for that buyer's payments to the artist (clause 6.1(a)). The card number is never seen by PlotArt or the artist.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.2\"><span class=\"n\">9.2</span><span>The artist's acceptance of this addendum, their seller-information confirmation, any processing consent, each withdrawal, and each delivery offer version are kept for six years after the artist leaves the basket, or for as long as any of the artist's basket orders is kept, whichever is later.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"10-leaving-the-basket\">10. Leaving the basket</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.1\"><span class=\"n\">10.1</span><span>The artist can leave the basket at any time in PlotArt Studio. Their artworks are then no longer offered in the basket. Baskets already paid, or being paid, are completed under this addendum.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.2\"><span class=\"n\">10.2</span><span>Leaving the basket does not affect the artist's agreement, their gallery listing, enquiries, direct sales, any PA-PAY quote, or anything owed to a buyer or by PlotArt under this addendum.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.3\"><span class=\"n\">10.3</span><span>PlotArt may pause or close the basket for everyone, or stop offering a particular artwork, with notice in PlotArt Studio. Baskets already paid, or being paid, are completed.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"11-changes\">11. Changes</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.1\"><span class=\"n\">11.1</span><span>PlotArt can change this addendum only by issuing a new version with its own identifier. A new version applies to the artist only when the artist expressly accepts it in PlotArt Studio. Until then, the artist's artworks remain offered under the version they accepted, or, if PlotArt can no longer offer them under it, are withdrawn from the basket without any other effect.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"12-test-mode-and-live-payments\">12. Test mode and live payments</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c12.1\"><span class=\"n\">12.1</span><span>PA-PAY clause 10 applies. Accepting this addendum, or any test version of it, in test mode does not authorise live payments. Before any live basket order, the artist must have joined the live payment pilot (PA-PAY), accept the issued live version of this addendum after it has been shown to them, confirm their seller information (clause 2.2), give the processing consent separately if they wish to offer commission-free artworks (clause 4), and complete Stripe's live onboarding, including payouts. No test-mode acceptance, confirmation, consent or account becomes a live one.</span></p>\n</article>\n<footer>PlotArt Artist Basket Addendum · PA-BAA-2026-11 · PlotArt, an initiative of PlotNua, operated by Colin MacAulay (registered as Colin Macaulay), CRO business name no. 794392 · plotnua.ie · hello@plotnua.ie</footer></main></body></html>\n"},"PA-BBT-2026-11":{"title":"PlotArt Basket Purchase Terms","kind":"buyer_basket_terms","html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en-IE\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>PlotArt Basket Purchase Terms · PA-BBT-2026-11</title><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex, nofollow\">\n<style>\n:root{color-scheme:light}body{margin:0;background:#F4F1EC;color:#1B1C1E;font:16px/1.6 Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1rem 4rem}.eyebrow{margin:0;color:#AE6245;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.8rem}\nh1{font:400 2.1rem/1.15 Georgia,serif;margin:.3rem 0 .4rem}.sub{margin:0 0 2rem;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.95rem}\nh2{font:400 1.3rem/1.3 Georgia,serif;margin:2.2rem 0 .7rem}p{margin:0 0 .8rem}.cl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem minmax(0,1fr)}\n.cl .n{font-weight:700}ul{margin:0 0 .9rem 3rem;padding-left:0;list-style:none}li{margin:0 0 .35rem}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:.6rem 0 1.4rem;font-size:.92rem}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border:1px solid #D8D1C7;padding:.55rem .65rem}\nthead th{background:#EFEBE5}tbody th{font-weight:400;width:60%}footer{margin-top:3rem;padding-top:1rem;border-top:1px solid #C9C2B8;color:#5E5A55;font-size:.85rem}\n@media (max-width:30rem){.cl{grid-template-columns:2.6rem minmax(0,1fr)}ul{margin-left:2.6rem}h1{font-size:1.75rem}}\n@media print{body{background:#fff}main{padding:0}}\n</style></head>\n<body><main><article data-doc=\"PA-BBT-2026-11\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">PLOTART</p>\n<h1>Basket Purchase Terms</h1>\n<p class=\"sub\">Identifier PA-BBT-2026-11 · Text of 21 November 2026</p>\n<p>These terms apply when you buy one or more original artworks together through the PlotArt basket. Each artwork in your basket is sold to you by its own artist.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-who-you-are-buying-from\">1. Who you are buying from</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.1\"><span class=\"n\">1.1</span><span><strong>Each artwork has its own seller.</strong> Each artwork in your basket is sold to you by the artist named with it, who is the seller of that artwork. You make a separate contract of sale with each seller, for each artwork. Before you pay, the basket page shows these details for each seller under &quot;Seller and returns information&quot;; your purchase confirmation repeats them:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) the seller's legal name and any trading name;</li><li>(b) the geographical address at which they are established, and any different address for returns and complaints;</li><li>(c) the seller's email and telephone number;</li><li>(d) the seller's VAT number, if they are registered.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.2\"><span class=\"n\">1.2</span><span><strong>The seller's declaration.</strong> Each seller has declared to PlotArt that they sell as a trader, in the course of their business, craft or profession. PlotArt offers the basket only for artworks whose seller has made that declaration. If you are buying as a consumer, you have consumer rights under EU consumer protection law for each artwork, including the right to cancel; section 7 explains how to cancel.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.3\"><span class=\"n\">1.3</span><span><strong>PlotArt's role.</strong> PlotArt (PlotNua, operated by Colin Macaulay, CRO business name no. 794392, hello@plotnua.ie) introduces you to the sellers. It shows the artworks, provides the basket and the checkout, and coordinates the payments. PlotArt is not the seller of any artwork.</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) Each seller is responsible for their artwork, its delivery, cancellations, returns and refunds, and for the artwork matching its description.</li><li>(b) PlotArt is responsible for the accuracy of the information it presents on the basket page and in your purchase confirmation, and for operating the basket and the checkout.</li><li>(c) PlotArt can receive your cancellation notice, complaint or damage report on any seller's behalf at hello@plotnua.ie, and will pass it on to that seller.</li><li>(d) <strong>PlotArt's commission.</strong> Some sellers pay PlotArt a commission out of the artwork price, under their own agreement with PlotArt; others pay none. A commission is never added to what you pay and does not change your rights.</li><li>(e) PlotArt selects and orders artists and artworks by hand, for curatorial reasons. No seller pays for placement.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c1.4\"><span class=\"n\">1.4</span><span><strong>One basket, separate purchases.</strong> Buying several artworks together does not make PlotArt, or any seller, responsible for another seller's artwork. Your rights for each artwork are against that artwork's seller, and are not affected by what happens to any other artwork in your basket, except as section 4.3 says for payment.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-what-you-pay\">2. What you pay</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.1\"><span class=\"n\">2.1</span><span>For each artwork, your basket page shows, in euro:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) the artwork price;</li><li>(b) separately, the seller's charge for packing, transport and transit insurance to your address in the Republic of Ireland;</li><li>(c) the total for that artwork.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.2\"><span class=\"n\">2.2</span><span>Your basket page also shows the total for all the artworks in your basket. Nothing else is added at checkout. PlotArt charges you no fee.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.3\"><span class=\"n\">2.3</span><span><strong>Where we deliver.</strong> The basket delivers only to addresses in the Republic of Ireland. For delivery elsewhere, please enquire about the artwork instead.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c2.4\"><span class=\"n\">2.4</span><span><strong>Prices are fixed when you pay.</strong> The price and delivery charge you are shown when you go to checkout are the amounts you pay. If either has changed since you added the artwork to your basket, the basket page shows the new amount before you continue, and you will not be charged an amount you were not shown.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-placing-your-order\">3. Placing your order</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.1\"><span class=\"n\">3.1</span><span><strong>Steps.</strong> To buy the artworks in your basket you:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) check the artworks, sellers, amounts, delivery and return arrangements on the basket page;</li><li>(b) give your name, email address and delivery address;</li><li>(c) confirm that you have read these terms;</li><li>(d) select &quot;Buy now&quot;, which shows the total you will pay, then enter your card on Stripe's secure page and select &quot;Save&quot; there. Selecting &quot;Save&quot; on Stripe's page completes your order, with an obligation to pay the total shown. Your card is saved only to take the payments for your basket.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.2\"><span class=\"n\">3.2</span><span>Until you select &quot;Save&quot; on Stripe's page, you can go back, correct your details or remove artworks, and nothing is bought. Your order is an offer to buy each artwork in your basket from its seller. Each contract of sale is made when your purchase is confirmed under section 4.4.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c3.3\"><span class=\"n\">3.3</span><span><strong>Limits.</strong> A basket can hold up to 10 artworks. PlotArt cannot arrange purchases of EUR 10,000 or more in total, including purchases that, together with other purchases by you or anyone PlotArt knows to be acting with you in the previous twelve months, reach that amount. An artwork priced at more than EUR 9,999.99 cannot be bought through the basket.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"4-payment\">4. Payment</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.1\"><span class=\"n\">4.1</span><span><strong>You enter your card once.</strong> You enter your card once, on Stripe's secure page. Stripe saves it for your basket so that PlotArt can make a separate card payment for each artwork, to that artwork's seller's own Stripe account. PlotArt does not hold your payments, and it is not an escrow arrangement.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.2\"><span class=\"n\">4.2</span><span><strong>On your card statement</strong>, each artwork appears as its own payment to its seller, so a basket of several artworks shows several payments. Your purchase confirmation lists each one.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.3\"><span class=\"n\">4.3</span><span><strong>All or nothing.</strong> PlotArt first asks your card issuer to authorise the payment for every artwork in your basket. Only when every payment has been authorised does PlotArt take them. If any payment cannot be authorised, for example because your card is declined or a seller can no longer accept payment:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) no artwork in your basket is bought, and no payment is taken;</li><li>(b) PlotArt cancels every authorisation already made. Your bank may show a cancelled authorisation as pending for a few days before it disappears; it is not a payment;</li><li>(c) the basket page tells you, and you can try again.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.4\"><span class=\"n\">4.4</span><span><strong>Your purchase is confirmed</strong> when every payment in your basket has been taken. The page you return to shows whether your purchase has been confirmed.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.5\"><span class=\"n\">4.5</span><span><strong>If your bank asks you to confirm a payment.</strong> Your bank may ask you to confirm one or more of the payments, for example in your banking app. The basket page shows this. If you do not confirm within 30 minutes, no artwork is bought and every authorisation is cancelled under section 4.3.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.6\"><span class=\"n\">4.6</span><span><strong>Your saved card.</strong> Your card is saved and used only for the payments in this basket. PlotArt does not use it for any other payment. Once your basket is completed or cancelled, PlotArt removes the saved card from use for future payments.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c4.7\"><span class=\"n\">4.7</span><span><strong>Your purchase confirmation.</strong> Once your purchase is confirmed, PlotArt prepares a purchase confirmation for each artwork. It sets out the artwork, the seller and their contact details, what you paid for it, the delivery and return arrangements, these terms in full and the model cancellation form. You can open each confirmation from your order page, and PlotArt keeps an exact copy. PlotArt also emails them to you at the address you gave, as your confirmation of each contract.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"5-one-original-holding-the-artworks\">5. One original; holding the artworks</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.1\"><span class=\"n\">5.1</span><span>Each original can be sold only once. When you select &quot;Checkout&quot;, PlotArt holds every artwork in your basket for you for the checkout period, currently 31 minutes, plus a short time for confirmation, and longer while your bank is asked to confirm a payment (section 4.5). While an artwork is held, no one else can buy it through PlotArt, and its seller has agreed not to sell or promise it elsewhere.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.2\"><span class=\"n\">5.2</span><span>An artwork in your basket is not held until you select &quot;Checkout&quot;. If it has been sold or become unavailable before then, the basket page tells you, and you can remove it and continue with the others.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c5.3\"><span class=\"n\">5.3</span><span>If, exceptionally, your payment is taken for an artwork that its seller had already sold another way, that seller refunds you in full for that artwork. Your purchases of the other artworks are not affected, unless you choose to cancel them under section 7.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"6-delivery-and-insurance\">6. Delivery and insurance</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.1\"><span class=\"n\">6.1</span><span>Each seller delivers their own artwork. Your artworks may therefore arrive separately, from different places and at different times. Before you pay, the basket page shows for each artwork its delivery charge, delivery window and tracking, that the shipment is insured, and the return arrangements. Your purchase confirmation sets out in full:</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) who packs and who transports the artwork;</li><li>(b) the delivery window and tracking;</li><li>(c) whether a signed receipt and condition photographs are provided;</li><li>(d) the transit insurance arranged for the shipment: the insured value (at least the artwork price), the period of cover and how a claim is made.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.2\"><span class=\"n\">6.2</span><span>The seller delivers to the address you gave, within the delivery window stated for that artwork. If a seller cannot deliver within that window, they will contact you, and you may agree a new date or end the contract for that artwork and be refunded in full for it.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c6.3\"><span class=\"n\">6.3</span><span>Please inspect each artwork when it arrives. If it is damaged, it helps if you tell its seller or PlotArt (hello@plotnua.ie) within 48 hours, with photographs, so that any insurance claim can be made promptly. This is a request, not a condition. Reporting later does not affect your rights under section 8.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"7-changing-your-mind-your-right-to-cancel\">7. Changing your mind: your right to cancel</h2>\n<p>This section applies if you are a consumer buying from a seller who is a trader (section 1.2).</p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.1\"><span class=\"n\">7.1</span><span><strong>Each artwork separately.</strong> You may cancel your purchase of any one or more artworks in your basket, and keep the others. Cancelling one artwork does not cancel any other.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.2\"><span class=\"n\">7.2</span><span><strong>Cancellation period.</strong> You may cancel without giving any reason within 14 days from the day you, or someone you name other than the carrier, receive that artwork. If you bought two or more artworks from the same seller in one basket and they arrive separately, the 14 days for each of them run from the day you receive the last of them.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.3\"><span class=\"n\">7.3</span><span><strong>How to cancel.</strong> Tell the seller of the artwork, or PlotArt on the seller's behalf (hello@plotnua.ie), that you have decided to cancel, saying which artwork or artworks. You can use the model cancellation form in section 12 or any other clear statement, for example by email. To meet the deadline, it is enough to send your notice before the cancellation period ends.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.4\"><span class=\"n\">7.4</span><span><strong>Returning an artwork.</strong></span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) Return the artwork to the returns address shown for it, by the return method shown for it, without undue delay and no later than 14 days after you tell its seller or PlotArt that you are cancelling.</li><li>(b) Unless the seller has said that they will collect it, you arrange the return.</li><li>(c) Because original artworks cannot normally be returned by post, you bear the cost of returning an artwork when you cancel for a change of mind. The basket page and your purchase confirmation state that cost for each artwork, or a reasonable estimate of the maximum cost. Please pack the work as it was delivered. We recommend insuring it for its value while it is in transit.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.5\"><span class=\"n\">7.5</span><span><strong>Your refund.</strong> The seller refunds everything you paid for that artwork, including its delivery charge, without undue delay and no later than 14 days after being told that you are cancelling.</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) The seller may withhold the refund until it has received the artwork back, or until you have shown that you have sent it back, whichever is earlier.</li><li>(b) The refund is made to the card you paid with, at no charge to you.</li><li>(c) Cancelling one artwork does not change the price or delivery charge of any artwork you keep.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c7.6\"><span class=\"n\">7.6</span><span><strong>Handling an artwork.</strong> You may handle an artwork as you would in a gallery to establish its nature and characteristics. You may be liable for any loss in its value that results from handling beyond that.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"8-if-an-artwork-is-damaged-faulty-or-not-as-described\">8. If an artwork is damaged, faulty or not as described</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.1\"><span class=\"n\">8.1</span><span>Each seller must supply an artwork that matches its description and the information on the basket page. Your rights in this section are separate from, and in addition to, your right to cancel in section 7.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.2\"><span class=\"n\">8.2</span><span>If an artwork arrives damaged, or is not as described, tell its seller or PlotArt. If you do so within 30 days of receiving it (or, if it was installed, of installation being completed), you may end the contract for that artwork and receive a full refund for it, including its delivery charge, to the card you paid with. You may instead ask for a repair or a replacement where that is possible. Your other legal remedies continue after that.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.3\"><span class=\"n\">8.3</span><span>In these cases the seller bears the cost of returning the artwork, or reimburses you if you have paid it. The seller tells you how the return will be arranged.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c8.4\"><span class=\"n\">8.4</span><span>None of this depends on any carrier or insurance claim being made or completed.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"9-refunds\">9. Refunds</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.1\"><span class=\"n\">9.1</span><span>Refunds are made per artwork, to your original card through Stripe, from the seller's own Stripe account. Your right to be repaid does not depend on how the seller's Stripe account is funded.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.2\"><span class=\"n\">9.2</span><span><strong>If a refund is pending.</strong> Stripe may hold a refund as pending until the seller's Stripe account can fund it. A pending refund has not been completed: you have not been repaid until Stripe completes it. While it is pending, the seller does not repay you another way as well, because you would then be repaid twice. The seller must make sure you are repaid within the time limits in sections 7 and 8.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.3\"><span class=\"n\">9.3</span><span>If Stripe cannot complete a refund, or reverses one it first confirmed (for example because your card was closed), you have not been repaid. The seller then repays you once, either by a new refund through Stripe or directly, for example by bank transfer, and PlotArt confirms it with you.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c9.4\"><span class=\"n\">9.4</span><span>PlotArt tells you when it becomes aware that a refund is pending, has failed or has been reversed. The notice is emailed to you and also appears on your order page.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"10-your-data\">10. Your data</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.1\"><span class=\"n\">10.1</span><span><strong>What PlotArt receives and keeps.</strong> PlotArt receives your name, email address and delivery address with your basket. If you paid, it keeps them and the order record for each artwork until 31 December of the sixth year after that order is settled (completed or fully refunded, with nothing outstanding), for accounting and legal reasons. If no payment was taken, it keeps them until two years after the basket ended. They are never deleted while a payment dispute about the order is open. PlotArt keeps them longer only under a legal hold for a specific reason, such as a dispute, claim or tax enquiry about the order, reviewed at least every 12 months. The record includes the exact basket page details you were shown, your acceptance of these terms and your purchase confirmations.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.2\"><span class=\"n\">10.2</span><span><strong>Stripe.</strong> Stripe processes your payment details under its own privacy policy.</span></p>\n<ul><li>(a) Your card number is entered only on Stripe's page and is never seen by PlotArt or any seller.</li><li>(b) To make a payment to each seller, Stripe saves your card on PlotArt's Stripe account and, for each seller, makes a copy of it on that seller's own Stripe account. These saved cards are used only for the payments in your basket (section 4.6).</li><li>(c) Payment details Stripe records, such as your name, email address, billing country, and card brand and last four digits, are visible to each seller in their Stripe account, for that seller's payments only.</li><li>(d) PlotArt's access to Stripe also lets it view these details: your name, email address and billing country, and your card's brand, country, type, expiry date and last four digits. PlotArt does not copy them into its own records, and looks at them only when needed for your order, for example to resolve a refund or a payment dispute. PlotArt sends your email address to Stripe at checkout.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.3\"><span class=\"n\">10.3</span><span><strong>The sellers.</strong> PlotArt shares with each seller only what that seller needs to deliver their artwork and handle any return: your name, delivery address and, where needed, your email address. A seller is not told what you bought from other sellers.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c10.4\"><span class=\"n\">10.4</span><span>See the section &quot;The PlotArt payment pilot&quot; in the PlotNua privacy notice at plotnua.ie/privacy.html.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"11-questions-complaints-and-law\">11. Questions, complaints and law</h2>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.1\"><span class=\"n\">11.1</span><span>Contact the seller of the artwork at the contact details on your purchase confirmation, or PlotArt at hello@plotnua.ie, quoting your basket or order reference.</span></p>\n<p class=\"cl\" id=\"c11.2\"><span class=\"n\">11.2</span><span>Irish law applies. If you are a consumer living elsewhere, you keep the protection of the mandatory rules of your own country.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"12-model-cancellation-form\">12. Model cancellation form</h2>\n<p>[Complete and return this form only if you wish to cancel the contract.]</p>\n<p>To [the seller's name, address and email, as shown on your purchase confirmation] — or to PlotArt on the seller's behalf, hello@plotnua.ie:</p>\n<p>I/We [*] hereby give notice that I/We [*] cancel my/our [*] contract of sale of the following goods [*]: [artwork title], order reference [order reference],</p>\n<p>Ordered on [*] / received on [*],</p>\n<p>Name of consumer(s),</p>\n<p>Address of consumer(s),</p>\n<p>Signature of consumer(s) (only if this form is notified on paper),</p>\n<p>Date</p>\n<p>[*] Delete as appropriate.</p>\n</article>\n<footer>PlotArt Basket Purchase Terms · PA-BBT-2026-11 · PlotArt, an initiative of PlotNua, operated by Colin MacAulay (registered as Colin Macaulay), CRO business name no. 794392 · plotnua.ie · hello@plotnua.ie</footer></main></body></html>\n"}};
